{"title":"Cantidades al comprar comida","summary":"Distinguir some, any, much, many y a lot of en compras y cocina.","theory_extra":"<h2>Objetivo</h2><p>Distinguir some, any, much, many y a lot of en compras y cocina.</p><h2>Explicación</h2><p>Some se usa frecuentemente en afirmaciones y ofrecimientos; any, en preguntas y negativas. Many acompaña nombres contables plurales y much, nombres incontables. A lot of funciona con ambos.</p><h2>Diálogo original</h2><p>Mia: Do we have any apples?<br>Leo: Yes, we have some apples.<br>Mia: How much milk is there?<br>Leo: Not much. Let's buy some.</p><div class=\"tip\">Practicá el diálogo en voz alta. Inventá dos respuestas nuevas y comprobá el orden de las palabras.</div><div class=\"warn\">No traduzcas mecánicamente desde el español: prestá atención a auxiliares y preposiciones.</div>","vocab":[["apple","manzana"],["milk","leche"],["bread","pan"],["bottle","botella"],["many","muchos"],["much","mucho"]],"exercises":[["mcq","We don't have ___ milk.",["some","any","many"],1,"Any es habitual en negativas."],["fill","How ___ apples do you need?",["many"],"Apples es contable plural."],["mcq","How ___ water is there?",["many","much","a"],1,"Water es incontable."],["order","Ordená la frase.","We have some fresh bread.","Some acompaña afirmaciones."],["listen","¿Qué falta comprar?","We have apples, but we don't have any milk.",["Manzanas","Leche","Pan"],1,"Don't have any milk."],["dictation","Escribí la pregunta.","Do you have any oranges?","Any se emplea en preguntas."],["fill","I'd like ___ tea, please.",["some"],"Some aparece en pedidos corteses."],["mcq","¿Cuál es correcta?",["many rice","much rice","a many rice"],1,"Rice es incontable."],["order","Ordená la pregunta.","How many bottles do we need?","Many con bottles, plural contable."],["speak","Pedí una cantidad.","I'd like some bread, please.","Some bread es una cantidad no especificada."]]}
